      "data": {
        "title": "The library's indexes rebuild themselves when a member changes",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "library-made-current",
          "nodeId": "library-made-current-rebuild-indexes"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "status": "todo",
        "body": "The library root and the contracts index read their members (a tile shows the member's name, description, glyph and how many pieces it has), so adding a node to a member made both stale, and the tests said so. The generators are in scripts/library now and are run by hand, in order (contracts index, then library root). A single command that rebuilds both, and a line in the check that tells you to, would stop this being something to remember. Found while adding the ways back.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1793211762730,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
