      "data": {
        "title": "One honest validity check, and a page that says what it does",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "library-made-current",
          "nodeId": "library-made-current-p2c-graph-validity"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "status": "done",
        "body": "Decided 2026-10-28: a saved file has exactly one root with the required fields; a graph with no root may be open but is not saveable; the old Graph contract is replaced by one short page, \"What makes a graph valid\", written from what the validator really does, shown to Michael before canon. Done: save is blocked for no root or missing root fields (all five save entry points, workspace saves too); the check is utils/rootValidation.js. Still to do: (1) one validator with two real modes, load (tolerant) and save: today the toolbar validates in load mode, so the \"warning on load, error on save\" tier does not exist; a strict save would refuse 918 of the 1,593 graphs on disk (mostly legacy class files, archives, older contracts), so decide what save may refuse before turning it on. (2) Ask for the name instead of refusing when only the name is missing. (3) Two roots: settled by Michael, 2026-10-28: a graph with two roots is one node existing across two files (same nodeId); the second root is informational and not counted. Only two roots in one file is wrong. (4) Rename the validator codes that still use retired words: DECLARATION_COUNT_INVALID, DECLARATION_MULTIPLE_ROOT, DECLARATION_ROOT_RELATIONSHIP_MISSING, LANDING_SURFACE_MULTIPLE (the ground), and remove the dictionary ones (DICTIONARY_MISSING_FILE, DICTIONARY_MISSING_VIEW, CLASS_AUTHORITY_MISSING_ENTRY). (5) The Root primitive still says a graph without a root is a \"fragment\" and that a graph never has two roots. Settled: a rootless graph is a workspace (no new word), and two roots are one node across two files. The new wording for the Meaning and Invariants sections is for Michael to approve. (6) Draft the page, then retire graph-contract and docs/twilite-native-graph-v1.md with it.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1793219056199,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        },
        "notes": "2026-10-29: \"What makes a graph valid\" is a canon page (documentation/contracts/graph/what-makes-a-graph-valid), listed in the contracts index in place of the Graph contract; the Graph contract and docs/twilite-native-graph-v1.md are retired (kept as reference); AGENTS.md points at the page; tests/graphValidityPage.test.js holds every code the page names to the validator. Left from the original list: the name prompt on save (its own task), and what save may refuse beyond the root (a strict save would refuse 918 of 1,593 graphs on disk)."
      }
    },
