      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "The stage pattern on the other fifteen primitives",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "library-made-current",
          "nodeId": "library-made-current-stage-other-primitives"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "status": "waiting",
        "body": "The Root primitive has the new poster (the ten sections on the stage with Content ports and a prev/next chain, no pins or legend, a \"← Primitives\" way back, plumbing hidden when browsing). Decide for the other fifteen: (A) sections on every stage, (B) keep each worked diagram of specimen cards, (C) sections on the stage and the diagram's idea moves to a real example route. My lean: A with C. Routes, sorted on 2026-10-28: real examples are edge-class (edges/surface), handle (handles/ring), property (identity-field), import-export (the Page Template), method (the Page Template), membrane (interface-frame-smoke); placeholders are content, edge, face, glyph and surface (all \"the Page Template\"), port (the Declaration Template), portal (the Root), script (a task graph) and specification (the Glyph primitive). Routes are optional now, and a page does not say which template it is made from. Show only real examples as a card on the stage; drop the placeholders. The primitive posters script skips the root; it needs a switch or a rewrite when the others change.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1793236307840,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        },
        "notes": "2026-10-28: all the primitives are staged (A with C), published and live. Waiting for Michael's review pass."
      }
