      "data": {
        "title": "Check that a fragment's root carries the node id its expansion names",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "library-made-current",
          "nodeId": "library-made-current-guard-expansion-id"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "status": "done",
        "body": "A node spread across two files is joined by the host's stand-in (an import with mode expand) and the same node id on the fragment's root. The validator checks only the host side (EXPANSION_BRIDGE_NODE_ID_REQUIRED). Add a warning when the fragment, once loaded, has a root with a different node id. Small, with a test.\n\nDONE 2026-10-30 (5a0f1774). Expanding a piece whose root has another node id was already refused (CONTEXT_INCOMPATIBLE), and the refusal names both ids (tested). What was missing was saying so before anything is pressed: a Fragment card now shows \"Incompatible\" and the reason on its face without being selected, from the same compatibility check the Expand button uses.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1793292706407,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
