      "data": {
        "title": "Warn when two open graphs share a root node id with no expansion between them",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "library-made-current",
          "nodeId": "library-made-current-guard-shared-node-id"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "status": "done",
        "body": "A shared node id says that two files are one node, and only an expansion makes that true. Two graphs that share one by accident (a copied file) are the bug the workspace frame used to hide. Warn in the workspace, naming both graphs. Small, with a test.\n\nDONE 2026-10-30 (5a0f1774). The workspace now says, once for each pair, when two open graphs carry the same root node id and neither holds a Fragment for the other, naming both (utils/sharedNodeIds.js, tests/sharedNodeIds.test.js). Checked live: a copy of the emitter opened beside a graph whose Bridge brought in the real emitter raised it. Pieces of one node, a Fragment either way, never raise it.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1793292706407,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
